Source: opencode-desktop
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ackerman-00 <quietcraft@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), binutils, xz-utils
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://opencode.ai

Package: opencode-desktop
Architecture: amd64
# Runtime set derived from the upstream payload's ELF NEEDED entries
# (verified per release via teardown-sweep ldd scan) plus the wrapper's
# helpers. t64 library names target Debian Testing (trixie and newer);
# libffmpeg.so is bundled inside /opt/OpenCode, libc6/libgcc-s1 cover the
# toolchain libs. Upstream's own Depends under-specifies this set.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libasound2t64, libatk1.0-0t64, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64, libatspi2.0-0, libc6, libcairo2, libcups2t64, libdbus-1-3, libexpat1, libgbm1, libgcc-s1, libglib2.0-0t64, libgtk-3-0t64, libnotify4, libnspr4, libnss3, libpango-1.0-0, libsecret-1-0, libstdc++6, libudev1, libuuid1, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxext6, libxfixes3, libxkbcommon0, libxrandr2, libxss1, libxtst6, ripgrep, xdg-utils
Recommends: libappindicator3-1
Description: Open source AI coding agent
 OpenCode is an open source agent that helps you write and run code with
 any AI model. This package repacks the upstream desktop build.
